.\"
.\" THR_SELF(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH THR_SELF 2 "May 2024" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
thr_self \- get the current thread ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/thr.h>
.PP
.BI "long thr_self(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR thr_self ()
returns the thread ID (TID) of the calling thread.
Each thread in the system has a unique TID.
The main thread of a process has a TID equal to the process's PID.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The ID of the current thread.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 432
Arguments:      None
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getpid (2),
.BR thr_new (2)
